# Phase 1 live MJPEG and concurrent API hardware test
# Date: 2026-11-22
# Board: AI-Thinker ESP32-CAM (original ESP32, OV2640), ESP32-CAM-MB
# Build: final focused MJPEG-chunking source; PlatformIO upload hash verified

## Result

Authenticated GET /camera/stream returned HTTP 200 with
multipart/x-mixed-replace; boundary=vcframe.

curl --max-time 10 observed:
  downloaded bytes: 613270
  JPEG SOI markers: 53
  JPEG EOI markers: 52
  multipart boundaries: 53

While the stream was open, authenticated GET /camera/status returned HTTP
200, 160 bytes, with camera initialized and sensor OV2640. curl exited with
code 28 at the intentional 10-second client timeout; the final frame was
therefore partial.

## UART excerpt

I (7587) vc_net: GOT_IP 10.151.183.4 (rssi -58 dBm, connects=1)
W (19167) httpd_txrx: httpd_sock_err: error in send : 104
W (19167) httpd_txrx: httpd_sock_err: error in send : 128
I (19177) vc_web: live stream ended after 9986 ms
W (19177) httpd_txrx: httpd_sock_err: error in recv : 104

The socket errors followed the client timeout/close; stream cleanup completed
after approximately 10 seconds. Browser-rendered frames on phone/laptop and
GPIO4 flash-off behavior on stream exit were not tested.
